{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1553660-w20-w5-w2e-abandoned-pack-seeks-new-storyteller","id":1553660,"title":"W20/W5/W2e Abandoned pack seeks new storyteller","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-09-05T22:17:22-07:00","id":1553660,"title":"W20/W5/W2e Abandoned pack seeks new storyteller","content":"Hello, we are a group of 5 players from all over the world that recently began an online game of Werewolf: The Apocalypse. Unfortunately, we have lost our GM after 2 short sessions. But the bond between packmates is strong, and we are looking for any GM to adopt us in our fight against the Wyrm. Presumably, we would be restarting the chronicle from scratch with you as storyteller.<br /> <br /> Presently, we are meeting on Sundays from 4-8 PM PST (11:00 to 15:00 GMT Monday) but we are somewhat flexible in terms of Sunday scheduling. Here is a short primer for our pack...<br /> <br /> <img width=\"223\" height=\"257\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/EUAjwAW.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/EUAjwAW.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/EUAjwAW.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> Chrissy Sinclair (Homid Silver Fangs Ahroun): This proud and haughty warchief has no time for her pack mate's games and vanity projects. She has refined her taste for luxury to be as sharp as her silver claws. She wears the pants and does the talking.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <img width=\"221\" height=\"323\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/pzX7B0l.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/pzX7B0l.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/pzX7B0l.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> Angus (Lupus Fianna Galliard): Our bard howls with rage as the vampire leaches spread their filth across Gaia with every bite. He alone knows the wickedness of a particularly nasty Kindred elder, and his hunt for them has brought him into our pack.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <img width=\"218\" height=\"267\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/V67u7yI.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/V67u7yI.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/V67u7yI.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> Silash Ashton (Homid Fianna Philodox): The pack's judge has keen eyes and a mysterious past. Angus has been his companion since he was a pup.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <img width=\"218\" height=\"305\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/gcb266L.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/gcb266L.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/gcb266L.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> John Forger (Homid Glass Walker Theurge): John will turn his technical genius towards any problem he can't solve by throwing money at. Owns a few cars and safehouses in all the places that matter. His umbral innovations have recently attracted unwanted attention from a few unseelie Fey.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <img width=\"216\" height=\"216\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/K9kX8X5.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/K9kX8X5.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/K9kX8X5.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> Air-Bud (Metis Bone Gnawer Ragabash): This sneaky little science experiment is on the lamb from the Technocracy. The scars from being a test subject have made him too ugly to look at, but not too ugly to SLAM DUNK!\u200b<br /> <br /> We are all somewhat flexible on the start time/day, as well as any major details for our characters. We DO want to ensure that we have all 3 breeds and all 5 auspices, but the rest is just details <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Send me a DM if you are interested on here or Discord (btl_simulations)<br /> <br /> We are online most evenings, and we'd love to hear from you! Cheers!<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28913-btl-simulations","name":"BTL.Simulations","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-06T00:21:23-07:00","id":1553661,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this is the best sub-forum for that. There's a place for this called <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings\">Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play</a>. Not a big deal on my book, though, I would just repost there to see if you get answers more easily.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately I can't help beyond some advice, but I think for this to work a primer on the players and their expectations is more important than one on the characters. That isn't bad, but not really the information a prospective Storyteller needs to think about the idea.<br /> <br /> And I have to say... this is no W5. Nothing against the flexibility to use several editions, but those characters simply aren't compatible with W5. 5th edition is a very different beast than any previous WtA game, and approaching it out of misplaced expectations won't do any good. There are no non-homids in W5. There are no Fianna, either. Even the other tribes are quite different. There are no Kin-folk. Not only those things don't exist in W5, in its setting they never existed. Quite a different game, one you may like or not, but not in any way, shape or form what your group is expecting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}